{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791589569,"nonce":"4Ja+PeOCde9iPB9kh3S5+0LHjDA=","message":"cn::tabs strip moved in place (4562453d): trigger colour and weight are computeds over the selected tab and hover, and cn-tabs-trigger--active follows the selection with class_when. Recorded from the old strip first and compared exactly; a separate test holds the strip to no rebuild under hover and press, and a tree-level one checks the stylesheet's --active rule moves between triggers. The content area still swaps its panel with a rebuild, because a panel is built only while shown.\n\nDecision recorded while doing it: a reactive class is on a node's class set only once the style passes have applied it, so with no stylesheet it is not there. Putting it there at build was tried and reverted: the base pass then bakes the class's rules into the node before the layer is recorded, and the layer could not be removed. Making membership independent of a stylesheet would mean hiding the class from every pass that matches classes (base, layout overrides, combined), and the snapshot order between the visual and layout passes is not fixed.\n\nSidebar, tree, select and combobox were read and left. Their rebuild is not a class or a colour: it changes which children exist (labels hidden when the rail is collapsed, a list of rows) and sits under animate_bounds, so it needs lazy branches and lists with a scope per row (746993e) before it can move.","files":null}]}